    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Bug\n\nSwitching from a busy Chat session to Terminal immediately selects destructive `interrupt`, cancelling the active tool/turn and queued instructions without a Finish-versus-Stop choice. The reverse Terminal-to-Chat direction already presents that policy dialog.\n\n**Source:** [ChatUI QA and regression harness PR #4419](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/4419)  \n**Reported by:** Dhruv Sharma via local native-Electron QA  \n**Analyzed against:** `d71acca1e13ddd9ab3a01a43f029853686f4c693`; exact hard-coded path remains on `04b676c9abd2fac4505081b0c099e079a30bde57`  \n**Environment:** macOS arm64, source-built AO, verified daemon on port 3001  \n**Priority:** P1 \u2014 active and queued work can be destroyed without consent  \n**Confidence:** High \u2014 reproduced natively and exact transition policy traced\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Start a Chat turn that runs a long tool, such as `sleep 20`.\n2. Optionally queue a follow-up.\n3. Click the top-bar action to switch to Terminal UI.\n4. Observe no policy dialog; the transition begins immediately.\n5. The native TUI shows the tool/turn as interrupted.\n\n## Expected\n\nIdle/no-queue Chat may drain directly. Active or queued Chat must show **Finish work, then switch** (safe default) versus **Stop now and switch**, name affected queue/draft state, and make no interrupt request before explicit consent.\n\n## Actual\n\nThe renderer sends `policy: interrupt` immediately and temporarily exposes a mismatched surface while the destructive transition runs.\n\n## Root cause\n\n- `frontend/src/renderer/components/SessionView.tsx:704` hard-codes `interrupt` for Chat-to-Terminal before checking busy/queued state.\n- `backend/internal/service/chat/controller.go:1389` applies interrupt semantics, cancelling the durable queue and provider work.\n\n## Fix direction\n\nReuse the existing policy dialog in both directions. Derive the safe default from active/queued state and prove no transition POST occurs before user choice.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Busy Chat always offers drain versus interrupt.\n- Default focus is **Finish work, then switch**.\n- Drain preserves accepted active/queued work.\n- Interrupt occurs only after explicit **Stop now** consent.\n- `npm run qa:chatui -- --grep MQA-05` passes in strict mode.\n\n## Evidence\n\n![Busy Chat switched directly to interrupted Terminal](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/b7d4a8dc8cf8843be42a3c0bb183e35103ccd06f/docs/qa/chatui-2026-08-25/screenshots/33-busy-chat-to-terminal-transition.png)\n\n- [Full finding](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/blob/b7d4a8dc8cf8843be42a3c0bb183e35103ccd06f/docs/qa/chatui-2026-08-25/manual-qa-report.md)\n\n## Related\n\n- [PR #3671](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/3671) \u2014 earlier symmetric policy-dialog behavior\n- [PR #3957](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/3957) \u2014 introduced unconditional Chat-to-Terminal interrupt behavior\n- [PR #4419](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/4419) \u2014 two deterministic MQA-05 policy contracts",
